      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Method",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Char the onion halves and ginger directly over a gas flame or under a very hot grill for 5 to 8 minutes, turning, until blackened in places.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Toast the star anise, cinnamon, and cloves in a dry pan for 1 minute until fragrant. Set aside.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Place the whole chicken in a large stockpot. Cover with 2.5 litres of cold water. Bring to the boil and skim off any foam.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Add the charred onion, ginger, and toasted spices. Reduce the heat to a low simmer. Cook for 45 to 60 minutes until the chicken is cooked through.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Remove the chicken and set aside to cool slightly. Strain the broth through a fine sieve. Return the broth to the pot.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Season the broth with fish sauce and sugar. Taste and adjust. It should be clear, fragrant, and lightly savoury.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Pull the chicken meat off the bones and slice or shred it. Discard the skin and bones.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Divide the cooked noodles between 4 bowls. Top with chicken, spring onion, and coriander. Ladle over the very hot broth.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Serve with bean sprouts, lime wedges, and sliced chilli on the side.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          }
        ],
        "type": "orderedList"
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "fix": "Skim foam thoroughly in the first 10 minutes and keep the heat at a very gentle simmer throughout.",
              "cause": "The soup boiled too vigorously or the foam was not skimmed.",
              "symptom": "The broth is cloudy instead of clear."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "fix": "Char the onion and ginger until quite blackened on the outside. This gives the broth its sweetness and colour.",
              "cause": "The onion and ginger were not charred enough.",
              "symptom": "The broth tastes bland and watery."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "fix": "Check the chicken after 45 minutes by piercing the thigh. Remove it from the broth as soon as it is cooked through.",
              "cause": "The whole chicken was simmered for too long.",
              "symptom": "The chicken breast meat is dry."
            }
          }
        ],
        "type": "troubleshooter"
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Where this dish lives",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Phở gà is most closely associated with Hanoi, where it developed alongside beef phở. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "It is considered a lighter and more elegant version of the classic soup. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "Northern Vietnamese cooks value the clarity of the broth and use fewer herbs than southern versions. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "In the south, phở is served with a large plate of herbs, sauces, and garnishes on the side. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "Both versions are eaten at breakfast, lunch, and dinner across the country.",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
      }
    ],
    "type": "doc"
  },
